From 405a6687d99abb0d10e9ff200de7c8a280a5948b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aibing Chen <chenaibing@cmss.chinamobile.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:04:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] thermal/debugfs: size the transition buffer for the worst
 case

cdev_tt_seq_show() formats a cooling device transition as "%d->%d" into a
11 byte buffer.  A transition packs two 16 bit state values into
entry->id, so the worst case is "65535->65535" plus the terminator, 13
bytes.  With -Wformat-truncation enabled for W=1 builds, and COMPILE_TEST
configurations turning the warning into an error through CONFIG_WERROR,
the file does not build:

  drivers/thermal/thermal_debugfs.c:331:59: error: '%d' directive output
    may be truncated writing between 1 and 5 bytes into a region of size
    between 3 and 8 [-Werror=format-truncation=]

Size the buffer for the packed state values.

Signed-off-by: Aibing Chen <chenaibing@cmss.chinamobile.com>
---
 drivers/thermal/thermal_debugfs.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/thermal/thermal_debugfs.c b/drivers/thermal/thermal_debugfs.c
index da02d8f17..9b3731b57 100644
--- a/drivers/thermal/thermal_debugfs.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/thermal_debugfs.c
@@ -323,10 +323,10 @@ static int cdev_tt_seq_show(struct seq_file *s, void *v)
 
 	list_for_each_entry(entry, &transitions[i], node) {
 		/*
-		 * Assuming maximum cdev states is 1024, the longer
-		 * string for a transition would be "1024->1024\0"
+		 * A transition packs two 16 bit state values, so the
+		 * longer string would be "65535->65535\0"
 		 */
-		char buffer[11];
+		char buffer[13];
 
 		snprintf(buffer, ARRAY_SIZE(buffer), "%d->%d",
 			 entry->id >> 16, entry->id & 0xFFFF);
